@@ -97,9 +105,23 @@ class Encoding:
         - Setting `allowed_special` to "all" will cause this function to treat all text
           corresponding to special tokens to be encoded as special tokens.
 
+        When `chunk_size` is set, the input text is first split into segments of at most
+        `chunk_size` characters, each segment is encoded independently, and the result is a
+        list of token lists, one per chunk. This is useful for processing long documents
+        within context limits. Any other per-input feature (e.g. `return_repeated_pattern`)
+        operates independently on each chunk.
+
+        When `return_repeated_pattern` is True, the top 3 most frequent adjacent token pairs
+        (with their occurrence counts) are tracked during encoding, and a dictionary mapping
+        each pair to its count is returned alongside the tokens.
+
         ```
         >>> enc.encode("hello world")
         [31373, 995]
+        >>> enc.encode("hello world", chunk_size=5)
+        [[31373], [995]]
+        >>> enc.encode("hello world", return_repeated_pattern=True)
+        ([31373, 995], {(31373, 995): 1})
         >>> enc.encode("<|endoftext|>", allowed_special={"<|endoftext|>"})
         [50256]
         >>> enc.encode("<|endoftext|>", allowed_special="all")
